  "conclusions": [
    {
      "text": "The preserved 17-row shoreline JSON inventory has 17 distinct GSHHG IDs and context counts Tristan 6, Gough 9, Bouvet 2. This is a count of the retained inventory, not proof of island/coastline completeness; this PR did not re-extract the large GSHHG archive.",
      "status": "supported",
      "source_ids": [
        "gshhg-2.3.7-prior-inventory"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The retained Natural Earth source geometry hashes differ from the pinned atlas geometries for both scoped subjects. This rejects the prior equality assertion, but does not decide whether atlas generalization is suitable.",
      "status": "supported",
      "source_ids": [
        "natural-earth-admin1-5.1.1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Natural Earth Admin-1 classification and the inspected official pages do not establish the legal boundary or WorldAtlas province/area purpose for these locations.",
      "status": "unresolved",
      "source_ids": [
        "natural-earth-admin1-5.1.1",
        "tristan-government-primary-pages",
        "norsk-polar-institute-bouvet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Completeness of current Tristan island-group representation and legal source-policy coverage remain unresolved; broader Tristan crosswalk work remains with issue #620.",
